#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hardware-passthrough.rst:2
msgid "Hardware Passthrough"
msgstr "Hardware Passthrough"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hardware-passthrough.rst:4
msgid ""
"|morpheus| includes hardware passthrough and pooling support for VMs "
"provisioned to |clusters|. This support extends to GPU, USB and NVME "
"devices. In order to be usable, such devices must be attached to a |host|"
" or to multiple |hosts|. |morpheus| includes controls to detach hardware "
"devices from the underlying OS on the hypervisor host and add them to a "
"pool where they are available for consumption by VMs. GPU hardware can be"
" attached to VMs at provision time through custom Service Plans or on an "
"ad-hoc basis by manually attaching hardware to existing VMs. Other "
"supported hardware types must be past through to the VM after "
"provisioning."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| incluye hardware passthrough y pooling support para VMs "
"aprovisionado a |clusters|. Este support extends a GPU, USB y NVME "
"devices. Para be usable, such devices debe be adjunto un un |host| o a "
"múltiples |hosts|. |morpheus| incluye controls a detach hardware devices "
"desde el underlying OS en el hypervisor host y agregar them a un pool "
"donde they están disponibles para consumption por VMs. GPU hardware puede"
" be adjunto un VMs en provision tiempo a través de personalizado Servicio"
" Plans o en un ad-hoc basis por manualmente attaching hardware a "
"existente VMs. Otro soportado hardware tipos debe be past a través de al "
"VM después de provisioning."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hardware-passthrough.rst:6
msgid ""
"This page describes whole-device passthrough. NVIDIA vGPU slicing keeps "
"the GPU bound to the NVIDIA Host driver and assigns programmed SR-IOV "
"virtual functions instead of the full physical card. For that workflow, "
"see :doc:`hvm/nvidia_vgpu`."
msgstr "Esta página describe el pass-through de dispositivo completo. El slicing de NVIDIA vGPU mantiene la GPU vinculada al controlador de host NVIDIA y asigna funciones virtuales SR-IOV programadas en lugar de la tarjeta física completa. Para ese flujo de trabajo, consulte :doc:`hvm/nvidia_vgpu`."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hardware-passthrough.rst:9
msgid "Creating Service Plans"
msgstr "Creating Service Plans"

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hardware-passthrough.rst:11
msgid ""
"When utilizing GPU hardware, it may be most convenient to use a custom "
"Service Plan. This allows administrators to pre-configure the number of "
"discrete hardware cards to attach to the VM at provision time. Once "
"provisioned, the specified number of GPUs will be attached to the VM. For"
" workloads which are provisioned and torn down regularly, this will save "
"additional steps of manually attaching GPUs available from the pool. On "
"teardown, attached devices of all types are released back to the pool. "
"Though in some cases utilizing Service Plans may be most convenient, as "
"you'll see in the next sections it is not strictly required. It is also "
"possible to manually attach GPUs or other hardware types on any existing "
"VM runnning on |clusters|."
msgstr ""
"Cuando utilizing GPU hardware, it puede be más convenient a usar un "
"personalizado Servicio Plan. Este permite administrators a pre-configure "
"el número de discrete hardware cards a attach al VM en provision tiempo. "
"Once aprovisionado, el specified número de GPUs será be adjunto un el VM."
" Para cargas de trabajo cual son aprovisionado y torn down regularly, "
"este será guardar adicional pasos de manualmente attaching GPUs "
"disponible desde el pool. En teardown, attached devices de todos tipos "
"son released back al pool. Though en algunos cases utilizing Servicio "
"Plans puede be más convenient, como you'll ver en el siguiente sections "
"it es no strictly requerido. It es también possible a manualmente attach "
"GPUs o otro hardware tipos en cualquier existente VM runnning en "
"|clusters|."

#: ../../infrastructure/clusters/hardware-passthrough.rst:13
msgid ""
"To create a new Service Plan, navigate to |AdmPla|. Click :guilabel:`+ "
"Add` and then Service Plan. In the New Service Plan modal, first set the "
"PROVISION TYPE configuration to \"KVM.\" This will update the available "
"configuration fields and reveal :guilabel:`GPU Count` and :guilabel:`GPU "
"Type`. Select a physical GPU Type for whole-card passthrough. Indented "
"Segment Types represent NVIDIA vGPU profiles and use the separate slicing"
" workflow. See :doc:`/administration/plans_pricing/plans` for complete "
"Service Plan guidance."
msgstr "Para crear un nuevo Plan de servicio, vaya a |AdmPla|. Haga clic en :guilabel:`+ Add` y luego en Service Plan. En el modal New Service Plan, primero configure PROVISION TYPE en \\\"KVM\\\". Esto actualizará los campos de configuración disponibles y mostrará :guilabel:`GPU Count` y :guilabel:`GPU Type`. Seleccione un GPU Type físico para pass-through de tarjeta completa. Los Segment Types con sangría representan perfiles de NVIDIA vGPU y utilizan el flujo de trabajo de slicing por separado. Consulte :doc:`/administration/plans_pricing/plans` para obtener orientación completa sobre Planes de servicio."

